<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE-South African budget tax revenue changes.</title>
<headline>TABLE-South African budget tax revenue changes.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table is a summary of the effect on revenue in fiscal 1997/98 of tax proposals made by South African Finance Minister Trevor Manuel in his budget on Wednesday:		    (rand million)</p>
<p>Restructuring of rates and brackets of personal income tax -2,800</p>
<p>Fringe benefits:</p>
<p>    Increase on company cars			 150</p>
<p>    Increase in private km			   100</p>
<p>    Travel allowance subject to PAYE		70</p>
<p>    Housing anti-avoidance			    50</p>
<p>Exemption levels:</p>
<p>    Scholarship or bursary			    -1</p>
<p>Tax on retirement funds:</p>
<p>Property unit trust dividends, manufactured interest and fees on scrip lending transactions		 200</p>
<p>Marketable securities:</p>
<p>    Reduction in rate				 -100</p>
<p>    Withdrawn exemption for foreigners	    50</p>
<p>Stamp duty:</p>
<p>    Reduction in rate				  -75</p>
<p>    Withdrawal of arbitrage exemption		0</p>
<p>Customs and excise:</p>
<p>Reduction in ad valorem duties to 15 pct  -150</p>
<p>    Increased tobacco, beer, wine duties	 798</p>
<p>    Fuel levy					    800</p>
<p>    TOTAL REVENUE CHANGE			    -908</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>-- Parliamentary newsroom +27 21 4032502</p>
